        {
          "id": "chem170_step1_lev25_bin4_h2so4",
          "description": "Reference: the em_scm_xy chem_opt = 170 column of data/eqwefic/chem170_scm (fork branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170, B20 fixed, GNU gfortran 13.3 REAL*4), dumped by the MOSAIC mass-transfer hook right after aerosolmtc at model step 1, level 25, size bin 4 of 8, gas H2SO4. Regime: T = 286.62 K, p = 0.7382 atm, wet diameter 5.449e-05 cm, number 4.595 /cm3. cond_rate is checked against the dumped non-volatile condensation rate for this bin, which the model forms as gas*kg independently of this component's own product. Tolerance measured, not assumed: over the twenty-five cases kg agrees with WRF to 3.9e-8 median and 1.7e-7 worst in a zero-tolerance run, and cond_rate to 3.7e-8 / 1.5e-7, so the bound is 5e-7. The kernel is double precision inside WRF (kind=8), so the residual is the single-precision storage of the dumped inputs and of kg itself, not the arithmetic.",
          "parameter_overrides": {
            "t_k": 286.6180725097656,
            "p_atm": 0.7382122278213501,
            "dp_wet": 5.4485306463902816e-05,
            "num_conc": 4.595207214355469,
